-- the least element of a list under a given rank, folded with the default as the running least: the
-- canonical representative of an orbit, chosen inside the orbit so that the choice is invariant.
--
-- The cost is why it is written this way. Taking the least as
--   case leb (rk y) (rk (min-by A rk r d)) of true → y; false → min-by A rk r d
-- names the recursive call twice, once in the scrutinee and once in the branch, so a step count for a
-- list of m elements satisfies T(m) = 2 T(m-1) + 1 and the whole computation is Theta(2^m) -- for an
-- orbit of nineteen atoms, half a million steps to pick a minimum of nineteen numbers. Folded with the
-- running least as the default, each element is visited once: T(m) = T(m-1) + 1, which is Theta(m).
-- The two forms agree wherever the default is itself in the list, which is every use here, since the
-- representative of an atom is taken with that atom as the default and an atom is in its own orbit.
min-by : (A : Type 0) → (A → Nat) → List A → A → A
min-by A rk xs d = case xs of
  nil → d
  cons y r → min-by A rk r (case leb (rk y) (rk d) of true → y; false → d)
